                <pb facs="0740" n="590" sameAs="frus:frus1907p2/pg590"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Subinclosure.—Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Brown to
                        Consular Agent Reed.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1907-06-11"><hi rendition="#italic">June 11,
                        1907</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Referring to yours of June 1 to Consul-General Kent, I would state for your
                    guidance that the American Government reserves to itself alone the right to
                    decide who are entitled to the protection of an American passport, and that in
                    any case of doubt it is expected the Guatemalan authorities will always show
                    consideration and await the final disposition of the case between this legation
                    and the Guatemalan Government.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Philip Brown.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
